<main class="wrap">
 <a class="back" href="/projects">← All projects</a>
 <div class="meta m"><span style="color:var(--ink)">Build 06</span><span class="ln"></span><span>Accessible reading · Responsible Computing Club, SJSU</span><span class="ln"></span><span><span class="rec" style="animation:none;background:var(--ink)"></span>Shipped · Spring 2026</span></div>

 <section class="top">
  <div>
   <h1 style="font-size:clamp(76px,12vw,184px)">Luminara</h1>
   <div class="kick">Dense writing in. Clear writing out. <span>Meaning kept.</span></div>
   <p class="lede">An app that makes academic reading accessible. Upload a PDF, slides, a Word doc or even a photo of a page, and Luminara finds the hard parts, rewrites only those with a local AI model, and hands the file back in its original format. I led the backend.</p>
   <div class="acts"><a class="pillb solid" href="#demo">Try the simplifier <span class="arr"></span></a><a class="pillb" href="#sketch">See the whiteboard</a><a class="pillb" href="https://github.com/Lord-Helix07/Luminara">Source</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="facts rv">
   <div><span>My role</span><span>Lead backend developer</span></div>
   <div><span>Also</span><span>Helped teammates with code &amp; Figma</span></div>
   <div><span>Team</span><span>6 · Responsible Computing Club</span></div>
   <div><span>AI</span><span>Local llama3 via Ollama</span></div>
   <div><span>Stack</span><span>Flask · spaCy · React · Docker</span></div>
  </div>
 </section>


 <section class="real">
  <div class="rv"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><span class="c bl"></span><span class="c br"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 01 · THE REAL APP</span><span class="or">● SCREENSHOT</span></div><img src="/img/lumui.jpg" alt="Luminara upload screen with output format, language, page range and accessibility options"><div class="ft"><span>DYSLEXIA FRIENDLY · TEXT-TO-SPEECH · SIMPLIFY</span><span>NOT STORED</span></div></div>
   <p><b>Upload and choose.</b> Pick an output format, a language and a page range, then turn on dyslexia-friendly mode, text-to-speech or simplification.</p></div>
  <div class="rv d1"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><span class="c bl"></span><span class="c br"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 02 · A REAL RUN</span><span class="or">● RECORDING</span></div><video src="/video/lumdemo.mp4" poster="/img/lumposter.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video><div class="ft"><span>PDF IN → CONVERTED → DOWNLOAD</span><span>RUNNING LOCALLY</span></div></div>
   <p><b>Convert and download.</b> A real speech-outline PDF goes through the backend, comes back as clean text with its structure kept, and downloads as a file again.</p></div>
 </section>

 <!-- 01 PROBLEM -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">01</span> · The problem</span><span>Who it's for</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">It's not the student. It's the text.</h2><p class="rv d1">Students struggle with academic reading not because they lack ability, but because <b>the content isn't accessible</b>. Three groups feel it the most.</p></div>
  <div class="aud">
   <div class="au rv"><span>01</span><h5>Dense text</h5><p>Long sentences and complex vocabulary overwhelm any reader.</p></div>
   <div class="au rv d1"><span>02</span><h5>ESL students</h5><p>International learners face an extra language barrier on every page.</p></div>
   <div class="au rv d2"><span>03</span><h5>Dyslexic learners</h5><p>Dense paragraphs make comprehension significantly harder.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="quote2 rv">Learning should be understandable for everyone, <em>regardless of background, language or learning style.</em></div>
 </section>

 <!-- 02 DEMO -->
 <section class="sec" id="demo">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">02</span> · How it feels</span><span>Try it</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Simplify the hard parts. Keep the rest.</h2><p class="rv d1">Luminara doesn't rewrite the whole page. It <b>flags only the difficult words and phrases</b>, replaces those, and leaves everything else exactly where it was. Tap a highlighted word to save it to your dictionary.</p></div>
  <div class="demo rv">
   <div class="dl">
    <div class="modes" id="modes"><button data-m="orig">Original</button><button class="on" data-m="flag">Flagged</button><button data-m="new">Luminara</button></div>
    <div class="doc mode-flag" id="doc"></div>
    <div class="meter"><span id="mlabel">FLAGGED WORDS · <b>6</b></span><span>ILLUSTRATIVE TEXT</span></div>
   </div>
   <div class="dr"><div class="m">My dictionary</div>
    <div class="dict" id="dict"><div class="empty">Tap any highlighted word to save it. Saved words are kept in mind the next time the model rewrites a page.</div></div>
    <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#3a3936;margin-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px"><b style="font-weight:500">Learn, don't just simplify.</b> Each entry has a part of speech and a clear definition, and the dictionary grows with the reader.</p></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 03 SKETCH -->
 <section class="sec" id="sketch">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">03</span> · The architecture</span><span>It started on a whiteboard</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">From a sketch to a seven-step pipeline.</h2><p class="rv d1">This is the real sketch I drew for the backend. The idea that shaped everything is in step four: <b>no full generation, only flags</b>. The AI never gets to rewrite the whole document.</p></div>
  <div class="sk rv">
   <div class="im"><img src="/img/sketch.jpg" alt="Hand-drawn Luminara backend pipeline sketch"><div class="cap">ORIGINAL SKETCH · FEB 23, 2026</div></div>
   <div class="steps7">
    <div class="s7"><span>01</span><div><h5>Upload</h5><p>PDF, slides or Word doc, with an edge check on the file.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7"><span>02</span><div><h5>Extract text</h5><p>Parse the file, save its type, convert to one common format.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7"><span>03</span><div><h5>Identify &amp; flag</h5><p>Find what's hard: for dyslexia, for language learners, or what the user asks.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7 key"><span>04</span><div><h5>Modify flags only</h5><p>Keep the theme. No full generation. Output replacements for flagged spans.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7"><span>05</span><div><h5>Rebuild</h5><p>Create the full text with the flags replaced.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7"><span>06</span><div><h5>Revert file type</h5><p>Reverse step two, so the output matches the input format.</p></div></div>
    <div class="s7"><span>07</span><div><h5>Output</h5><p>Download, rasterize if needed, and delete the user's file.</p></div></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 04 MY PART -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">04</span> · What I built</span><span>The backend</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">The engine underneath the app.</h2><p class="rv d1">I was the main backend developer: the Flask server and everything it does with a file. I also <b>helped teammates write their code and design in Figma</b>, so the whole team could ship together.</p></div>
  <div class="mine">
   <div class="mp rv"><span class="n">01 · FILES</span><h5>Any format in, same format out</h5><p>PDFs, slides, Word docs and photos of pages, with OCR for images, converted to text and back again.</p><div class="t">PyMuPDF · pytesseract · python-pptx · python-docx · Pillow</div></div>
   <div class="mp rv d1"><span class="n">02 · NLP</span><h5>Find what's hard</h5><p>Readability scoring and word-rarity checks flag difficult spans before any AI runs.</p><div class="t">spaCy · textstat · wordfreq</div></div>
   <div class="mp rv d2"><span class="n">03 · LOCAL AI</span><h5>Rewrite only the flags</h5><p>A local llama3 model replaces just the flagged spans, guided by the reader's saved words.</p><div class="t">Ollama · llama3</div></div>
   <div class="mp rv"><span class="n">04 · SECURITY</span><h5>Accounts that hold up</h5><p>JWT sign-in that blocks disposable emails, caps password length against malicious input, and rate-limits login attempts.</p><div class="t">Flask · PyJWT</div></div>
   <div class="mp rv d1"><span class="n">05 · API</span><h5>Personal dictionary</h5><p>Save, list and delete words with their part of speech and definition, tied to each user.</p><div class="t">Flask · Flask-CORS</div></div>
   <div class="mp rv d2"><span class="n">06 · SHIP</span><h5>One-command setup</h5><p>Frontend, backend and the AI model all start together with Docker Compose.</p><div class="t">Docker · Docker Compose</div></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 05 FEEDBACK -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">05</span> · Listening to users</span><span>Demo feedback</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Users told us it was too simple. So we changed the goal.</h2><p class="rv d1">After the demo, people liked the idea but said the output lost important meaning, and they wanted help understanding hard words, not just removing them. <b>We shifted from shortening text to helping people understand it.</b></p></div>
  <div class="fb">
   <div class="fbc rv"><h5>WHAT WE HEARD</h5>
    <div class="fbr"><small class="or">WORKED</small><span>Simplifying dense academic text</span></div>
    <div class="fbr"><small style="color:var(--mut)">DIDN'T</small><span>Output got too simple and lost meaning</span></div>
    <div class="fbr"><small style="color:var(--mut)">MISSING</small><span>Help learning hard words, and better dyslexia support</span></div></div>
   <div class="arrowc">→</div>
   <div class="fbc after rv d1"><h5>WHAT WE CHANGED</h5>
    <div class="fbr"><small>MEANING</small><span>Keep the original meaning while simplifying</span></div>
    <div class="fbr"><small>BALANCE</small><span>Less aggressive rewrites, so details stay</span></div>
    <div class="fbr"><small>LEARNING</small><span>Built the personal dictionary</span></div></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 06 CHALLENGES -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">06</span> · Hard parts</span><span>Tested on real textbooks</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Real textbooks, not sample data.</h2><p class="rv d1">We tested with real textbooks from our own classes across several subjects, checking both readability and whether the meaning survived. <b>Real text exposed problems sample data never would.</b></p></div>
  <div class="ch3">
   <div class="rv"><small>01 · SCORING</small><h5>Unreliable readability scores</h5><p>Flesch-Kincaid scores swung with text length, causing over- and under-flagging.</p></div>
   <div class="rv d1"><small>02 · FORMAT</small><h5>Keeping the layout</h5><p>Headers and titles had to stay in place while still being simplified when needed.</p></div>
   <div class="rv d2"><small>03 · INTEGRATION</small><h5>Frontend ↔ backend</h5><p>CORS and port issues between React and Flask, including the dictionary calls.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="note rv"><div class="m">Responsible design</div><p>We <b>limited how much we used AI</b>. Cheaper, greener NLP does the flagging, and a local model does only the rewriting, so documents never have to leave the machine.</p></div>
 </section>

